I18N.add({"1 · Municipio by municipio":"1 · Municipio por municipio","2 · What a municipio map can show":"2 · Lo que un mapa por municipio puede mostrar","3 · Hazard Mitigation: approved, obligated and awaiting a decision":"3 · Mitigación de Riesgos: aprobado, obligado y en espera de decisión","3D + Time":"3D + Tiempo","4 · HUD grants: CDBG-DR, CDBG-MIT and yearly CDBG":"4 · HUD grants: CDBG-DR, CDBG-MIT and yearly CDBG","<b>Census Bureau Community Resilience Estimates.</b> Municipio table, as published on the map's Environment tab. US Government work.":"<b>Estimaciones de Resiliencia Comunitaria del Negociado del Censo.</b> Tabla por municipio, tal como se publica en la pestaña Ambiente del mapa. Obra del Gobierno de EE. UU.","<b>Data and method.</b> The data file is data/public_money_need.json (public_money_need.py), built only from the observatory's published data files; the method is in docs/analysis/public-money-v2-2026-10/ of the project repository.":"<b>Datos y método.</b> El archivo de datos es data/public_money_need.json (public_money_need.py), construido solo con los archivos de datos publicados del observatorio; el método está en docs/analysis/public-money-v2-2026-10/ del repositorio del proyecto.","<b>FEMA National Risk Index.</b> County table, expected annual loss, as published on the map's Environment tab. US Government work.":"<b>Índice Nacional de Riesgo de FEMA.</b> Tabla por condado, pérdida anual esperada, tal como se publica en la pestaña Ambiente del mapa. Obra del Gobierno de EE. UU.","<b>HUD money per resident.</b> The same 2020 Census residents, over federal fiscal years 2019 to 2025 (October to September), by the year HUD obligated the money. CDBG-DR and CDBG-MIT: the subawards of the Department of Housing's disaster grants, by the municipio where the work is done. Yearly CDBG: the entitlement grants by the municipio that receives them, plus the CDBG state program's subawards by municipio; COVID-19 grants (CDBG-CV) are left out. Subawards are part of the prime grants and are never added to them, nor to FEMA's money.":"<b>HUD money per resident.</b> The same 2020 Census residents, over federal fiscal years 2019 to 2025 (October to September), by the year HUD obligated the money. CDBG-DR and CDBG-MIT: the subawards of the Department of Housing's disaster grants, by the municipio where the work is done. Yearly CDBG: the entitlement grants by the municipio that receives them, plus the CDBG state program's subawards by municipio; COVID-19 grants (CDBG-CV) are left out. Subawards are part of the prime grants and are never added to them, nor to FEMA's money.","<b>How to cite this page.</b> Foundation for Puerto Rico, Knowledge Area: Disaster funding and need, PR Data Observatory, Snapshot 2026-11 (draft). Data: FEMA (OpenFEMA, National Risk Index), USAspending.gov and U.S. Census Bureau (Community Resilience Estimates, 2020 Census).":"<b>Cómo citar esta página.</b> Foundation for Puerto Rico, Área de conocimiento: Fondos por desastres y necesidad, Observatorio de Datos de PR, Snapshot 2026-11 (borrador). Datos: FEMA (OpenFEMA, Índice Nacional de Riesgo), USAspending.gov y Negociado del Censo de EE. UU. (Estimaciones de Resiliencia Comunitaria, Censo 2020).","<b>In review:</b> the content of this page is under review and may change.":"<b>En revisión:</b> el contenido de esta página está en revisión y puede cambiar.","<b>Money per resident.</b> For each municipio, the dollars of each program from 2017 to 2025 are added, then divided by its residents in the 2020 Census. Public Assistance: federal share obligated, by applicant and the year the disaster was declared. Individual Assistance: dollars approved for owners and renters, by the year the disaster was declared. Hazard Mitigation: federal share approved, by benefiting municipio and fiscal year of the grant. The three FEMA programs together add the three; approved and obligated are different steps, so the sum is a rough total.":"<b>Dinero por residente.</b> Para cada municipio se suman los dólares de cada programa de 2017 a 2025 y se dividen entre sus residentes en el Censo 2020. Asistencia Pública: parte federal obligada, por solicitante y el año en que se declaró el desastre. Asistencia Individual: dólares aprobados para dueños e inquilinos, por el año en que se declaró el desastre. Mitigación de Riesgos: parte federal aprobada, por municipio beneficiado y año fiscal de la subvención. Los tres programas de FEMA juntos suman los tres; aprobado y obligado son pasos distintos, así que la suma es un total aproximado.","<b>Need.</b> Expected annual loss: FEMA's National Risk Index (December 2025) estimate of the average dollars lost each year to buildings, agriculture and lives from 18 natural hazards, divided by residents. It is higher where there is more to lose, so it reflects the value of what is exposed as well as the hazard. Residents with three or more risk factors: the Census Bureau's Community Resilience Estimates (2024), the share of residents with three or more of ten factors such as poverty, disability, no vehicle or no health insurance. The two measures are never combined.":"<b>Necesidad.</b> Pérdida anual esperada: el estimado del Índice Nacional de Riesgo de FEMA (diciembre de 2025) del promedio de dólares que se pierden cada año en edificios, agricultura y vidas por 18 amenazas naturales, dividido entre los residentes. Es mayor donde hay más que perder, así que refleja el valor de lo expuesto además de la amenaza. Residentes con tres o más factores de riesgo: las Estimaciones de Resiliencia Comunitaria del Negociado del Censo (2024), la parte de los residentes con tres o más de diez factores, como pobreza, discapacidad, no tener vehículo o no tener seguro médico. Las dos medidas nunca se combinan.","<b>OpenFEMA.</b> Public Assistance Funded Projects Details, Hazard Mitigation Assistance Subapplications and Housing Assistance Data (owners and renters), as published on the map (Home) and the Housing page. US Government work; OpenFEMA terms apply.":"<b>OpenFEMA.</b> Public Assistance Funded Projects Details, Hazard Mitigation Assistance Subapplications y Housing Assistance Data (dueños e inquilinos), tal como se publican en el mapa (Inicio) y en la página de Vivienda. Obra del Gobierno de EE. UU.; aplican los términos de OpenFEMA.","<b>Read with care.</b> This page states facts and draws no conclusions. Money obligated or approved is not money spent. Most FEMA Public Assistance cannot be placed in a municipio: 22% of it is on this map, the rest is recorded as statewide (power, water and Commonwealth agencies). Expected annual loss is a model estimate, not a record of losses. A municipio can rank high on money because of one large project.":"<b>Lea con cuidado.</b> Esta página presenta hechos y no saca conclusiones. El dinero obligado o aprobado no es dinero gastado. La mayor parte de la Asistencia Pública de FEMA no se puede ubicar en un municipio: el 22 % está en este mapa; el resto se registra como estatal (energía, agua y agencias del Gobierno de Puerto Rico). La pérdida anual esperada es un estimado de un modelo, no un registro de pérdidas. Un municipio puede quedar alto en dinero por un solo proyecto grande.","<b>Thirds and medians.</b> The 78 municipios are ranked on each measure and cut into three groups of 26 (terciles). The rank correlation (Spearman) compares the two orders: 1 when they agree, 0 when they are unrelated, below 0 when they run opposite. The medians split the 78 into two halves of 39.":"<b>Tercios y medianas.</b> Los 78 municipios se ordenan en cada medida y se dividen en tres grupos de 26 (terciles). La correlación de rangos (Spearman) compara ambos órdenes: 1 cuando coinciden, 0 cuando no se relacionan, menos de 0 cuando van en sentido contrario. Las medianas dividen los 78 en dos mitades de 39.","<b>USAspending.gov.</b> HUD's CDBG grants to Puerto Rico (assistance listings 14.218 and 14.228) and the subawards reported under the federal transparency law (FFATA), read from USAspending's API by cdbg_dr.py and cdbg_regular.py, as published on the Public spending page. US Government work; USAspending states no license for the data.":"<b>USAspending.gov.</b> HUD's CDBG grants to Puerto Rico (assistance listings 14.218 and 14.228) and the subawards reported under the federal transparency law (FFATA), read from USAspending's API by cdbg_dr.py and cdbg_regular.py, as published on the Public spending page. US Government work; USAspending states no license for the data.","<b>What the page does not do.</b> It does not say how much money a municipio should have received, rank municipios as better or worse, or explain why the money went where it did.":"<b>Lo que la página no hace.</b> No dice cuánto dinero debió recibir un municipio, no clasifica los municipios como mejores o peores ni explica por qué el dinero fue a donde fue.","A rank correlation near 0 means the order of the municipios by money says little about their order by need; near 1, the two orders agree; below 0, they run opposite.":"Una correlación de rangos cercana a 0 significa que el orden de los municipios por dinero dice poco sobre su orden por necesidad; cercana a 1, ambos órdenes coinciden; menor que 0, van en sentido contrario.","About":"Acerca de","About: this initiative, how to use the Observatory, terms":"Acerca de: esta iniciativa, cómo usar el Observatorio y los términos","Above the median in money and in need: {hh} municipios. Above in money, below in need: {hl}. Below in money, above in need: {lh}. Below in both: {ll}. Rank correlation: {rho}.":"Sobre la mediana en dinero y en necesidad: {hh} municipios. Sobre la mediana en dinero y bajo ella en necesidad: {hl}. Bajo la mediana en dinero y sobre ella en necesidad: {lh}. Bajo la mediana en ambos: {ll}. Correlación de rangos: {rho}.","All areas":"Todas las áreas","All of Knowledge, with search":"Todo Conocimiento, con búsqueda","All published files, with their sources and licenses":"Todos los archivos publicados, con sus fuentes y licencias","Any geography":"Cualquier geografía","Any license":"Cualquier licencia","Any year":"Cualquier año","Approved subapplications":"Subsolicitudes aprobadas","Areas":"Áreas","Ask":"Preguntar","Ask the observatory":"Preguntar al observatorio","Awaiting a FEMA decision":"En espera de una decisión de FEMA","Back to Puerto Rico":"Volver a Puerto Rico","Barrio":"Barrio","Before 2000":"Antes de 2000","Bivariate map: {money} and {need}, by municipio":"Mapa bivariado: {money} y {need}, por municipio","CDBG entitlement grant":"CDBG entitlement grant","CDBG state program subawards":"CDBG state program subawards","CDBG yearly grants, per resident":"CDBG yearly grants, per resident","CDBG-DR and CDBG-MIT subawards":"CDBG-DR and CDBG-MIT subawards","CDBG-DR and CDBG-MIT, per resident":"CDBG-DR and CDBG-MIT, per resident","Census block":"Bloque censal","Census block group":"Grupo de bloques","Census tract":"Sector censal","Covers year":"Incluye el año","Data":"Datos","Data Dictionary":"Diccionario de datos","Data Dictionary: meanings, sources, licenses, how to cite":"Diccionario de datos: significados, fuentes, licencias y cómo citar","Data dictionary":"Diccionario de datos","Data dictionary: meanings, sources, licenses, how to cite":"Diccionario de datos: significados, fuentes, licencias y cómo citar","Data used on this page":"Datos que usa esta página","Data: every dataset, map layer and set of places":"Datos: todos los conjuntos de datos, capas del mapa y grupos de lugares","Disaster funding and need by municipio":"Fondos por desastres y necesidad por municipio","Download CSV":"Descargar CSV","Draft prepared with the help of Claude (artificial intelligence).":"Borrador preparado con ayuda de Claude (inteligencia artificial).","Each dot is a municipio, in the color it has on the map. Need runs across and money per resident runs up, on a scale where each step is ten times the one below, because a few municipios have many times the median; values under $10 are drawn at $10. The dashed lines are the medians of the 78. Select a dot to see the municipio's figures.":"Cada punto es un municipio, con el color que tiene en el mapa. La necesidad va de izquierda a derecha y el dinero por residente de abajo hacia arriba, en una escala donde cada paso es diez veces el de abajo, porque unos pocos municipios tienen muchas veces la mediana; los valores menores de 10 $ se dibujan en 10 $. Las líneas discontinuas son las medianas de los 78. Seleccione un punto para ver las cifras del municipio.","Each municipio falls in a third (tercile) of the 78 by money per resident and in a third by need, so the map has nine colors. Dark red: more need and less money than most; blue: more money and less need; dark brown: high in both. The color compares municipios with each other, not with a standard of what is enough.":"Cada municipio cae en un tercio (tercil) de los 78 por dinero por residente y en un tercio por necesidad, así que el mapa tiene nueve colores. Rojo oscuro: más necesidad y menos dinero que la mayoría; azul: más dinero y menos necesidad; marrón oscuro: alto en ambos. El color compara los municipios entre sí, no con una norma de lo que es suficiente.","Each square counts the municipios. Thirds of money per resident: below {a}, from {a} to below {b}, {b} or more. Thirds of need: below {c}, from {c} to below {d}, {d} or more.":"Cada cuadro cuenta los municipios. Tercios de dinero por residente: menos de {a}, de {a} a menos de {b}, {b} o más. Tercios de necesidad: menos de {c}, de {c} a menos de {d}, {d} o más.","Expected annual loss from natural hazards ($ a year)":"Pérdida anual esperada por amenazas naturales ($ al año)","Expected annual loss from natural hazards, per resident":"Pérdida anual esperada por amenazas naturales, por residente","FEMA Hazard Mitigation approved":"Mitigación de Riesgos de FEMA aprobada","FEMA Hazard Mitigation by benefiting municipio, fiscal years 2017 to 2025":"Mitigación de Riesgos de FEMA por municipio beneficiado, años fiscales 2017 a 2025","FEMA Individual Assistance approved":"Asistencia Individual de FEMA aprobada","FEMA Public Assistance obligated":"Asistencia Pública de FEMA obligada","FEMA records Public Assistance by the applicant. When the applicant is the Puerto Rico Electric Power Authority, the Aqueduct and Sewer Authority or another Commonwealth agency, the money is recorded for the whole island and cannot be placed in a municipio. Individual Assistance is placed by the household's address. Hazard Mitigation is placed by the municipios a project benefits; a project that benefits several is split equally among them. Each bar shows its own years:":"FEMA registra la Asistencia Pública por el solicitante. Cuando el solicitante es la Autoridad de Energía Eléctrica, la Autoridad de Acueductos y Alcantarillados u otra agencia del Gobierno de Puerto Rico, el dinero se registra para toda la isla y no se puede ubicar en un municipio. La Asistencia Individual se ubica por la dirección del hogar. La Mitigación de Riesgos se ubica por los municipios que beneficia un proyecto; un proyecto que beneficia a varios se divide en partes iguales entre ellos. Cada barra muestra sus propios años:","FPR Research in Data: The State of Housing":"FPR Research in Data: El estado de la vivienda","FPR's own":"Propia de FPR","Federal disaster and community development money and two measures of need, by municipio":"El dinero federal para desastres y desarrollo comunitario y dos medidas de necesidad, por municipio","Federal disaster and community development money per resident by municipio, set next to two measures of need: expected loss from natural hazards and residents with three or more risk factors. Facts only, with what the data can and cannot place.":"El dinero federal para desastres y desarrollo comunitario por residente en cada municipio, junto a dos medidas de necesidad: la pérdida esperada por amenazas naturales y los residentes con tres o más factores de riesgo. Solo hechos, con lo que los datos pueden y no pueden ubicar.","Federal money obligated":"Dinero federal obligado","Federal share approved":"Parte federal aprobada","Foundation for Puerto Rico, Whole Community Resilience Planning (WCRP) program, list of 2026-10-06":"Foundation for Puerto Rico, programa Whole Community Resilience Planning (WCRP), lista del 6 de octubre de 2026","Foundation for Puerto Rico. PR Data Observatory home":"Foundation for Puerto Rico. Inicio del Observatorio de Datos de PR","Go to {area}":"Ir a {area}","Grid":"Cuadrícula","HUD CDBG yearly grants":"HUD CDBG yearly grants","HUD CDBG-DR and CDBG-MIT subawards":"HUD CDBG-DR and CDBG-MIT subawards","HUD CDBG-DR, CDBG-MIT and yearly CDBG by municipio, federal fiscal years {y}":"HUD CDBG-DR, CDBG-MIT and yearly CDBG by municipio, federal fiscal years {y}","HUD grants":"HUD grants","HUD's Community Development Block Grants reach Puerto Rico in three ways. The disaster recovery and mitigation grants (CDBG-DR and CDBG-MIT) go to the Puerto Rico Department of Housing: HUD obligated $19.10 billion of them in federal fiscal years 2019 to 2025, and the Department reported $4.90 billion in subawards to municipalities, contractors and nonprofits, $4.33 billion of it with a municipio. The yearly grants go straight from HUD to 27 larger municipios (entitlement grants, $222 million) and, for the other municipios, to the Department of Housing as the CDBG state program ($160 million), which passes it on as subawards. Subawards often arrive a year or more after the grant, so the latest year can show little. Obligated is not spent. Select a column heading to sort.":"HUD's Community Development Block Grants reach Puerto Rico in three ways. The disaster recovery and mitigation grants (CDBG-DR and CDBG-MIT) go to the Puerto Rico Department of Housing: HUD obligated $19.10 billion of them in federal fiscal years 2019 to 2025, and the Department reported $4.90 billion in subawards to municipalities, contractors and nonprofits, $4.33 billion of it with a municipio. The yearly grants go straight from HUD to 27 larger municipios (entitlement grants, $222 million) and, for the other municipios, to the Department of Housing as the CDBG state program ($160 million), which passes it on as subawards. Subawards often arrive a year or more after the grant, so the latest year can show little. Obligated is not spent. Select a column heading to sort.","HUD's grants are placed through the subawards the Puerto Rico Department of Housing reports, and the yearly entitlement grants through the municipio that receives them. Money the Department keeps for its own programs, has not passed on yet, or reports with no municipio is not placed.":"HUD's grants are placed through the subawards the Puerto Rico Department of Housing reports, and the yearly entitlement grants through the municipio that receives them. Money the Department keeps for its own programs, has not passed on yet, or reports with no municipio is not placed.","Hazard Mitigation":"Mitigación de Riesgos","Hazard Mitigation pays for projects and plans that reduce future disaster losses. For fiscal years 2017 to 2025, FEMA approved a federal share of $3.67 billion for Puerto Rico and has obligated $0.77 billion of it (21%); FEMA obligates money in steps as projects meet their milestones. Another $1.06 billion has been requested and awaits a FEMA decision. Of the 1,134 Hazard Mitigation subapplications FEMA lists for Puerto Rico in all years and statuses, it reports a payment for 163, too few to show money paid. Select a column heading to sort.":"La Mitigación de Riesgos paga proyectos y planes que reducen las pérdidas de desastres futuros. Para los años fiscales 2017 a 2025, FEMA aprobó una parte federal de 3.67 mil millones de dólares para Puerto Rico y ha obligado 0.77 mil millones (21 %); FEMA obliga el dinero por etapas, según los proyectos cumplen sus hitos. Otros 1.06 mil millones se han solicitado y esperan una decisión de FEMA. De las 1,134 subsolicitudes de Mitigación de Riesgos que FEMA lista para Puerto Rico en todos los años y estados, informa un pago para 163, muy pocas para mostrar el dinero pagado. Seleccione el título de una columna para ordenar.","Housing":"Vivienda","How to cite this page":"Cómo citar esta página","Immersive 3D + time view":"Vista inmersiva en 3D y tiempo","In review":"En revisión","In review · {who}":"En revisión · {who}","Key: money per resident in thirds, from bottom to top, and need in thirds, from left to right; each square says how many municipios":"Leyenda: dinero por residente en tercios, de abajo hacia arriba, y necesidad en tercios, de izquierda a derecha; cada cuadro dice cuántos municipios","Knowledge":"Conocimiento","Knowledge Area":"Área de conocimiento","Knowledge Area · Disaster funding and need":"Área de conocimiento · Fondos por desastres y necesidad","Knowledge Area · Public money":"Área de conocimiento · Dinero público","Knowledge: FPR studies, analyses and tools":"Conocimiento: estudios, análisis y herramientas de FPR","Learn":"Aprende","Learn: short lessons about maps and spatial analysis":"Aprende: lecciones cortas sobre mapas y análisis espacial","Led by {name}":"Dirige: {name}","License not stated":"Licencia sin declarar","License of the sources (strictest)":"Licencia de las fuentes (la más restrictiva)","Licensed, not open":"Con licencia, no abierta","Lines (routes)":"Líneas (rutas)","Map":"Mapa","Map Gallery":"Galería de mapas","Map Gallery: ready-made maps, topics and your saved maps":"Galería de mapas: mapas preparados, temas y sus mapas guardados","Map legend":"Leyenda del mapa","Map: every layer and tool, in 2D or 3D":"Mapa: todas las capas y herramientas, en 2D o 3D","Median money per resident":"Mediana del dinero por residente","Median need":"Mediana de la necesidad","Method":"Método","Money":"Dinero","Money and need":"Dinero y necesidad","Money: {m}. Need: {n}.":"Dinero: {m}. Necesidad: {n}.","Municipality":"Municipio","Municipio":"Municipio","Municipio by municipio":"Municipio por municipio","Need":"Necesidad","Network":"Red","Obligated as a share of approved":"Obligado como parte de lo aprobado","On this page":"En esta página","Open license":"Licencia abierta","Open license, with conditions":"Licencia abierta, con condiciones","Open the map":"Abrir el mapa","PR Data Observatory home":"Inicio del Observatorio de Datos de PR","PR Data Observatory · Foundation for Puerto Rico":"Observatorio de Datos de PR · Foundation for Puerto Rico","Plan approved by the Puerto Rico Department of Housing":"Plan aprobado por el Departamento de la Vivienda de Puerto Rico","Plan in progress":"Plan en proceso","Point at coordinates the plan gives":"Punto en las coordenadas que da el plan","Point at the OpenStreetMap place or landmark":"Punto en el lugar o hito de OpenStreetMap","Point at the town center":"Punto en el centro del pueblo","Point inside the Census barrio":"Punto dentro del barrio del Censo","Point inside the Comunidad Especial (Junta de Planificación, 2006)":"Punto dentro de la Comunidad Especial (Junta de Planificación, 2006)","Points (places, stops)":"Puntos (lugares, paradas)","Projections (after {year})":"Proyecciones (después de {year})","Puerto Rico":"Puerto Rico","Puerto Rico (its own total, with what is statewide)":"Puerto Rico (su propio total, con lo estatal)","Puerto Rico (the prime grants, with what is not placed)":"Puerto Rico (las subvenciones principales, con lo que no está ubicado)","Rank correlation (Spearman) between the two":"Correlación de rangos (Spearman) entre ambos","Region":"Región","Related":"Relacionado","Related and data":"Relacionado y datos","Residents (2020 Census)":"Residentes (Censo 2020)","Residents with three or more risk factors":"Residentes con tres o más factores de riesgo","Scatter plot: each dot is a municipio; dashed lines mark the medians":"Gráfica de dispersión: cada punto es un municipio; las líneas discontinuas marcan las medianas","Select a municipio on the map or in the chart for its figures.":"Seleccione un municipio en el mapa o en la gráfica para ver sus cifras.","Share of each program placed in a municipio":"Parte de cada programa ubicada en un municipio","Skip to the content":"Ir al contenido","Snapshot {date}":"Corte {date}","Sources":"Fuentes","Sources and licenses":"Fuentes y licencias","The chat could not be loaded. Check your connection and try again.":"El chat no pudo cargar. Revise su conexión e inténtelo de nuevo.","The data could not be loaded ({error}). Check your connection and reload.":"No se pudieron cargar los datos ({error}). Verifique su conexión y vuelva a cargar la página.","The page also shows HUD's Community Development Block Grants (CDBG): the disaster recovery and mitigation grants (CDBG-DR and CDBG-MIT) and the yearly grants, as obligated in federal fiscal years 2019 to 2025. HUD's money is never added to FEMA's: the years are counted differently. Pick it under Money, or see section 4.":"The page also shows HUD's Community Development Block Grants (CDBG): the disaster recovery and mitigation grants (CDBG-DR and CDBG-MIT) and the yearly grants, as obligated in federal fiscal years 2019 to 2025. HUD's money is never added to FEMA's: the years are counted differently. Pick it under Money, or see section 4.","The plan's own boundary is in its PDF map.":"El límite del propio plan está en su mapa en PDF.","The three FEMA programs together":"Los tres programas de FEMA juntos","Third of money (1 to 3)":"Tercio de dinero (1 a 3)","Third of need (1 to 3)":"Tercio de necesidad (1 a 3)","This knowledge area is in review and will be published when the review is complete.":"Esta área de conocimiento está en revisión y se publicará cuando concluya.","This topic on the map":"Este tema en el mapa","Updated {month}":"Actualizado: {month}","Views":"Vistas","WCRP":"WCRP","WCRP community":"Comunidad WCRP","WCRP region: {region}":"Región WCRP: {region}","What is this?":"¿Qué es esto?","What the map can show":"Lo que el mapa puede mostrar","Where federal disaster money per resident and two measures of need line up, and where they do not. The FEMA money is what FEMA obligated or approved for disasters declared, or grants of fiscal years, 2017 to 2025; it is divided by each municipio's residents in the 2020 Census. COVID-19 relief is not included.":"Dónde coinciden el dinero federal para desastres por residente y dos medidas de necesidad, y dónde no. El dinero de FEMA es lo que FEMA obligó o aprobó para desastres declarados, o subvenciones de los años fiscales, de 2017 a 2025; se divide entre los residentes de cada municipio en el Censo 2020. No incluye la ayuda por el COVID-19.","Whole island":"Toda la isla","Workflows":"Flujos","Workflows: steps that turn data into a result on the map":"Flujos de trabajo: pasos que convierten datos en un resultado en el mapa","billion":"mil millones","lower third":"tercio inferior","middle third":"tercio medio","million":"millones","placed in a municipio (on the map)":"ubicado en un municipio (en el mapa)","recorded as statewide or not placed":"registrado como estatal o sin ubicar","upper third":"tercio superior","{a} to {b}":"{a} a {b}","{money}, per resident":"{money}, por residente","{name}: {money} per resident; {need}":"{name}: {money} por residente; {need}","{name}: {money} per resident; {need}. {cell} Select for the figures.":"{name}: {money} por residente; {need}. {cell} Seleccione para ver las cifras.","{n} layer on":["{n} capa activa","{n} capas activas"],"{p} of {total}":"{p} de {total}","{total} ({per} per resident)":"{total} ({per} por residente)"});
